{"title":"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Dick Gibbs</i>) For a given positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> find, in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> for which there is a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f2789508227865dfc89fd46e18ae9b25bff34257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> distinct positive integers that has sum greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> but every subset of size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has sum at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aaaf0b4d3eb080111baaa27f0fbe68d2057df81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let one optimal set of integers be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25be2b05853798c22ab4ab60c533a908b2472fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_1,\\dots,a_{2k+1}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4dfeb15bede16297ab46a8c9898f7342d47703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &gt; a_2 &gt; \\cdots &gt; a_{2k+1} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"202\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>The two conditions can now be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47a9caa3fa1e16b6f7484e6c0c65079ef0fe942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+\\cdots + a_k \\leq N/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e68f57b6019aa8ad567d4643fb529f57e85992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+\\cdots +a_{2k+1} &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />.\nSubtracting, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/345a237f7e9e421ecc1b93c2f0191d21bdaf6c5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}+\\cdots + a_{2k+1} &gt; N/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"18\" />, and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9ba1c6a1f79217018edae1d86eb06386cd4c24e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}+\\cdots + a_{2k+1} &gt; a_1+\\cdots + a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"265\" height=\"14\" />.\nIn words, the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> smallest numbers must exceed the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> largest ones.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b283e867398e250df1a3d74f3bcc2d209a23a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}=C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />. As all the numbers are distinct integers, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffe908a3bafd461d62ab6a53e8c2e59a0fdacdf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall i \\in\\{1,\\dots,k\\}:~ a_{k+1-i} \\geq C+i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />, and also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5829b6a6a2d2cfa92fa9cad97211416e5a85a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall i \\in\\{1,\\dots,k\\}:~ a_{k+1+i} \\leq C-i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"252\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f12ef21a6efeb176aeab4f9ebcaeaaf291502100.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+\\cdots + a_k \\geq kC + \\dfrac{k(k+1)}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"239\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edfce3f3f91726a42e01f99d9f17bd05f7fc9c1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}+\\cdots + a_{2k+1} \\leq (k+1)C - \\dfrac{k(k+1)}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"325\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>As we want the second sum to be larger, clearly we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14fe900a166dfd0087a3da7355f1a03e8f30b043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1)C - \\dfrac{k(k+1)}2 &gt; kC + \\dfrac{k(k+1)}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"300\" height=\"38\" />.\nThis simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a2885f96e62b974df6cb78a0075ca1d6fe5cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C &gt; k(k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Hence we get that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b1fd9933a602ee33842aa41fd2d070b59de47ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} N &amp; \\geq 2(a_1+\\cdots + a_k) \\\\   &amp; \\geq 2\\left( kC + \\dfrac{k(k+1)}2 \\right) \\\\   &amp; = 2kC + k(k+1) \\\\   &amp; \\geq 2k(k^2+k+1) + k(k+1) \\\\   &amp; = 2k^3 + 3k^2 + 3k \\end{align*}\" width=\"240\" height=\"146\" />\n</p><p>On the other hand, for the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/057225e2bca826018c8cb87afca9c1f0f670d93c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ k^2+k+1+i ~|~ i\\in\\{-k,\\dots,k\\} \\, \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"19\" /> the sum of the largest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> elements is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9ec8abfc31e4f7d8af52ccdc8cfad8dab57ca6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^3 + k^2 + k + \\dfrac{k(k+1)}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"179\" height=\"38\" />, and the sum of the entire set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fdad3c788f513480399923cb457b75ffa0ce50cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k^2+k+1)(2k+1) = 2k^3 + 3k^2 + 3k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"334\" height=\"21\" />, which is more than twice the sum of the largest set.\n</p><p>Hence the smallest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/7/447375f18f44ce3107e3c20d066c61f866b5d591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ N = 2k^3 + 3k^2 + 3k }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"169\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?t=84550 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO\" title=\"2006 USAMO\">2006 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017212203\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 198/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1663/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5755/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.829      1 -total\n 38.11%    6.413      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 31.74%    5.341      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 28.53%    4.802      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3184:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017212203 and revision id 62736. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}